{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe project pins Opus 4.8, Sonnet 4.6 and Haiku 4.5 (`rebar.toml`, `.github/llm-providers/*.toml`). Bedrock (896586841071/us-east-1) serves the 5.5 inference profiles. The epic lands this first, on the current engine.\n\nA bare id swap is unsafe. On 5.5: forced `tool_choice` `any`/`tool` returns 400 (Opus, Sonnet); thinking cannot be disabled (Opus); non-default sampling parameters return 400; assistant prefill returns 400; `effort` defaults to `medium` on Opus and Haiku. `pydantic-ai-slim` 1.107.9 (`profiles/anthropic.py::anthropic_model_profile`) does not list 5.5 ids, so its profile wrongly allows sampling for them.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Riskiest assumption first.** rebar's calls carry no forced tool choice, thinking toggle or prefill, so only sampling and effort need code. Code supports it: `structured.output_mode` (`src/rebar/llm/structured.py:149`) returns only `NativeOutput` or `PromptedOutput`; `capabilities._REBAR_OVERRIDES` (`src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py:214`) pins Claude to `native_structured_output=False`, so Claude always takes `PromptedOutput` (no tool, no prefill); no caller sets `RunRequest.thinking=True` (`src/rebar/llm/runner.py:93`); agentic loops leave `tool_choice` at `auto`. Step 1 tests this on the wire before other edits: `python -m rebar.llm.evals.provider_parity --probe` (`provider_parity.py:589`) for the two slots `CLASS_SLOTS` defines (`frontier`, `standard`), plus `provider_parity.probe_slot(\"us.anthropic.claude-haiku-5-5\")` for Haiku, which has no parity slot; each probe sends a bare call and a `temperature=0` call, and every 400 is recorded.\n\n**Ids and tables.** Replace 4.x ids with the 5.5 ids verbatim (direct `claude-opus-5-5`, `claude-sonnet-5-5`, `claude-haiku-5-5`; Bedrock `us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5`, `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5`, `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-5-5`). These are exactly what `aws bedrock list-inference-profiles --profile frontier --region us-east-1` returned on 2026-11-09; unlike Haiku 4.5's dated profile (`capabilities.py:246`), Haiku 5.5's has no suffix. They go in the three toml files, `config.DEFAULT_MODEL`/`VERIFIER_DEFAULT_MODEL` (`src/rebar/llm/config.py:61,67`), `model_classes.TRIVIAL_DEFAULT_MODEL` and `MODEL_WINDOW_LADDER` (`src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py:45,62-66`; Haiku 5.5 window 1M), `review_kernel/verify.py::MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS` (`:294-297`; Haiku 5.5 128K), `bedrock_model.DEFAULT_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` (`:22`), `provider_parity.CLASS_SLOTS` (`:103-106`). The deploy defaults in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` and the alarm dimensions in `infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf` move in the sibling task `itchy-neutral-whooper`. `sizing._RUNG_CLASSES` (`plan_review/sizing.py:240`) keys on family substrings; no change.\n\n**Sampling.** Add each 5.5 id (bare, `us.`, `global.`) to `_MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES` (`capabilities.py:223`) with `supports_temperature: False`, the mechanism already used for Opus 4.7/4.8, so `structured_run.build_model_settings` (`:400-404`) omits Pass-2 `temperature=0`.\n\n**Effort, explicit.** rebar sends no `effort` today (no `effort`/`output_config` key is set anywhere under `src/rebar/llm`), so Opus 4.8 and Sonnet 4.6 run at the API default, which Anthropic's model documentation gives as `high` for every current model except Opus 5.5 and Haiku 5.5 (both `medium`). To keep the gate's reasoning depth unchanged across the upgrade, one per-model table beside the overrides pins `high` for Opus 5.5 and Sonnet 5.5 and `medium` for Haiku 5.5 (its default; Haiku 4.5 had no effort parameter). `structured_run.build_model_settings` and `agent_call.build_agent_kwargs` send it through pydantic-ai 1.107.9's provider-scoped settings: `anthropic_effort` on direct Anthropic, which `AnthropicModel` copies into `output_config.effort` unconditionally (`pydantic_ai/models/anthropic.py:1960-1978`; the profile flag only gates the thinking-derived fallback), and `bedrock_additional_model_requests_fields={\"output_config\": {\"effort\": ...}}` on Bedrock (`pydantic_ai/models/bedrock.py:338`, merged at `:706`). The Step-1 probe is extended to send one call with each setting and record that the request is accepted. No profile override is needed: rebar never requests a forced tool, and sampling is withdrawn by the override table above.\n\n**Cache minimum.** Add the three direct 5.5 ids to `_MODEL_CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS` (`capabilities.py:38`) at 512.\n\n**Audit.** Walk every model call site (`runner.py`, `structured_run.py`, `agent_call.py`, `anthropic_model.py`, `bedrock_model.py`, `providers.py` (read only), `review_kernel/`, `plan_review/passes.py`, `workflow/`) against the five changes plus the `refusal` stop reason, and record one row per check (site, finding, fix or \"not affected\") as a ticket comment. Anything needing more than these seams is filed as a bug linked `discovered_from`.\n\nThese seams already shape every call, so correcting them corrects every pass without touching the passes. The eval-spec `model:` pins move in the sibling task `real-pubescent-turnstone` (see links).\n\n## Scope\n\n- rebar.toml, .github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml, .github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml\n- src/rebar/llm/config.py, model_classes.py, capabilities.py, structured_run.py, agent_call.py, bedrock_model.py\n- src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py, src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/provider_parity_results.json\n- tests that pin the changed ids or values (4.x ids in files that also name the changed constants): tests/unit/test_capabilities.py, test_project_default_provider.py, test_model_classes.py, test_bedrock_provider.py, test_cache_floor_per_model.py, test_code_review_verifier_class.py, test_config_llm.py, test_llm_config_gate_root.py, test_llm_model_env_removal.py, test_pass1_finder_model.py, test_plan_review.py, test_provider_parity.py, test_pydantic_ai_runner.py, test_verifier_class.py, tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_recovery_context_product_bound.py, tests/unit/workflow/test_review_output_budget.py, tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py. Value changes beyond the id swap: Haiku window 200K to 1M and Haiku max output 64K to 128K, so expected constants change with the ids.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: each 5.5 id reports `supports_temperature=False` and a 512 cache minimum; a 5.5 Bedrock request carries `output_config.effort` and no `temperature`; a direct one carries `anthropic_effort`.\n- Edge: an unmapped id keeps family defaults (no effort sent, temperature kept); `sizing` maps `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-5-5` to `trivial`.\n- Live: provider-parity probe and full run once on 4.x before the change and once on 5.5 after, `AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `git grep -nE 'claude-(opus-4-8|sonnet-4-6|haiku-4-5)' -- rebar.toml .github/llm-providers src/rebar/llm/config.py src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py` prints nothing (every file whose ids this change replaces).\n- [ ] The model-call audit is a ticket comment with one row per call site and API change.\n- [ ] Every incompatibility the audit finds is fixed here or filed as a linked bug.\n- [ ] The capability and settings-builder tests under Testing pass.\n- [ ] The probe's bare call is accepted for the `frontier` and `standard` parity slots and for `probe_slot(\"us.anthropic.claude-haiku-5-5\")`, recorded in a ticket comment.\n- [ ] A call carrying the pinned `effort` is accepted on each 5.5 model on Bedrock, recorded in the same comment.\n- [ ] The before and after provider-parity results are recorded in a ticket comment.\n- [ ] The 5.5 provider-parity run reports `invalid: false` for both slots.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794257744568248001,"uuid":"7b691d94-f3a8-47a0-b918-c19a6e325c9a"}